<%# What the total is made of, next to the button that pays it.

    This is the payroll-review shape - Gusto, Square Payroll and Stripe all break a total into its
    components beside the control that commits it, because that is the one moment the split is worth
    reading. It is not a summary of the table's rows in the table's own terms, so it is not table rows;
    and it is not a card of its own, because the page had six surfaces and this is part of the finalize
    decision, not a thing beside it.

    The three keys are the three transactions `DistributeEarnings` writes, so this is also what each
    student's statement will show, not a presentation-only grouping.

    No total line: the sentence above already names it, and the confirmation names it again at the
    commitment. A fourth copy would be a fourth place to disagree. %>
<%= tag.dl id: "finalize-breakdown", class: "mt-4 max-w-xs space-y-1 text-sm" do %>
  <% { attendance: "Attendance, including bonuses", math: "Math", reading: "Reading" }.each do |reason, label| %>
    <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
      <dt class="text-slate-600"><%= label %></dt>
      <dd class="tabular-nums text-slate-900"><%= number_to_currency(earnings.totals_by_reason[reason] / 100.0) %></dd>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
